Clip Factory

Portions of clipfactory/detect/signals.py, clipfactory/twitch/recorder.py and
clipfactory/media/render.py are Python ports of, and adaptations from,
skills/3-editing/clip-stream (lib/moments.mjs, lib/live.mjs, lib/layouts.mjs) in
https://github.com/alisadiq-ai/favstash-ai-video-editing-skills
Copyright the FavStash authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Changes: ported to Python/numpy,
French-language normalization and lexicon, repeat/emote signals, reaction
typology, automatic facecam detection, face tracking, streamlink 8 log format.

Test fixture image: "astronaut" from scikit-image (NASA photograph, public domain).
French test voice: Piper fr_FR-siwis-medium (downloaded at test time, not redistributed).

clipfactory/media/face.py: TripodCamera is adapted from SmoothedCameraman in
https://github.com/mutonby/openshorts (MIT License).
clipfactory/media/models/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx: YuNet face detector
from https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo (Apache License 2.0), obtained from
https://huggingface.co/opencv/face_detection_yunet.
Scene detection uses PySceneDetect (BSD-3-Clause) as a library.
